rca of the issue:
OVERLAY STACKING BUG. Structure in _layout.tsx L149-208:
  <ScrollView>
    {convMenu && <Pressable overlay style={{position:'absolute',inset:0,zIndex:100}}/>}
    {convGroups.map(g => <View key={g.label}> /* static, no z-index */
      {items.map(c => <View convItemWrap /* position:'relative', zIndex:200 iff convMenu===c.id */ />)}
    </View>)}
  </ScrollView>
CSS stacking: the group <View> is `position:static` so it does not participate in the sibling stacking context with the overlay. Inside the ScrollView the paint order is (overlay z:100) then (group View z:auto → treated as 0). The nested convItemWrap's z:200 has NO effect at the ScrollView level (a stacking context created by a static ancestor is scoped inside that ancestor). Consequence: the overlay is painted ABOVE the entire group subtree, including the dropdown, for the vertical range the overlay actually covers. Empirically the overlay's rendered box covers roughly the first ~400px of the ScrollView content area, so top items (y≈186) are blocked and bottom items (y≈604) are not. FIX: (a) hoist the overlay to be a sibling of the ScrollView (or of the whole sidebar) with position:'fixed' (web) / position:'absolute' at root, OR (b) give each group <View> `position:'relative'` and `zIndex:200` when convMenu is inside it, OR (c) render the dropdown itself as a portal/Modal on web.
